The total number of flowers is $10 \times 20 = 200$.
The number of bloomed flowers is $\frac{4}{5}$ of 200, which is $160$.

\boxed{160}

The distance Tom travels out is $10 \text{ mph} \times 3 \text{ hours} = 30 \text{ miles}$.
To travel back 30 miles at 6 mph, it takes $30 / 6 = 5$ hours.

\boxed{5}

The total time required is 180 minutes (3 hours). To have the cake ready by 5:00 pm, Jordan needs to start 3 hours earlier.

5:00 pm minus 3 hours is 2:00 pm.

\boxed{2:00 \text{ pm}}

The code confirms that if Azibo scored 5 points, then Bahati scored 25 (5 + 20) and Dinar scored 15 (25 - 10). The total is 5 + 25 + 15 = 45, which matches the problem statement.

Azibo scored 5 points.

\boxed{5}
